local-changes: none besides the patches

Where and why. The pin of west.yml (Zephyr af17c0c8, 2026-07-29) has no BCM2710 SoC
and no Zero 2 W board; upstream added them on 2026-08-17 (40222de576b) and moving the
pin for one board is not wanted (docs/notes/pre-study-rpi-zero-2w.md, section 9.2).
These are Zephyr material, not a library: they are read by Zephyr's build as an
out-of-tree board, SoC, devicetree and driver root, so they live in the yakogl-drivers
Zephyr module (driver/zephyr/module.yml), whose board_root, soc_root and dts_root are
driver/ and which already carries the Verdin, NanoPC-T6 and STM32MP257F-DK boards and
SoCs that way. Every file keeps its upstream path relative to driver/ (dts_root's
include/ is where the devicetree finds the dt-bindings headers), so this list is
also the list of upstream paths. driver/zephyr/Kconfig sources
drivers/interrupt_controller/Kconfig.brcm and driver/zephyr/CMakeLists.txt compiles
the two controllers, as upstream's drivers/interrupt_controller/ does, and puts
include/ on the include path for <zephyr/drivers/interrupt_controller/intc_bcm283x.h>.
Not third_party/: Zephyr finds these files only in a module root.

Left out (upstream has them; not needed to build and boot to a console with the pin):
the board's doc/ (index.rst, img/rpi_zero_2w.webp); the bindings and drivers of the
nodes the board enables but hello_world does not use: brcm,bcm2835-rng
(drivers/entropy/entropy_bcm2835_rng.c), raspberrypi,bcm283x-vc-thermal
(drivers/sensor/broadcom/), raspberrypi,bcm283x-power
(drivers/power_domain/power_domain_rpi_bcm283x.c; the board's Kconfig.defconfig
turns POWER_DOMAIN on only with PM), and brcm,bcm2835-dma (drivers/dma/, the node is
disabled); a node without a binding is parsed and ignored. Upstream's
brcm,bcm283x-aux-uart binding and its uart_ns16550.c variant (patch 0002), the
framebuffer binding and driver changes (patch 0003), and the SMP support of
ee3207193d2 (arch/arm64 IPI hook, drivers/pm_cpu_ops spin-table; patch 0001) are
core changes the pin lacks and are not carried.

